==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is an [[Aku Altar (Enemy Base)|Aku Altar]].
*1 [[Henry]] spawns as the boss after 5 seconds<sup>150f</sup>.
*2 [[Dolphina]]s spawn after 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>, delay 46.67~50 seconds<sup>1,400f~1,500f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Celeboodle]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 26.67~40 seconds<sup>800f~1,200f</sup>.
*8 [[Aku Doge]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
*3 [[Condemned Peng]]s spawn after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>, delay 36.67~40 seconds<sup>1,100f~1,200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The main threat of this level is Henry, so any [[:Category:Cats with Freeze Immunity|Freeze Immune]] (namely [[Li'l Tank Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Eraser]] and, if acquired, [[Ancient Egg: N005 (Special Cat)|Hitman Cat]]) and nimble (namely [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]], [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman]], [[Talents|Talented]] [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can]] and [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser]]) cats are helpful. If you can sneak an attacker who can kill Dolphina and Condemned Pengs past Henry, you have already won. Celeboodles are good for money and you should kill the first one with a cat with the [[Extra Money]] ability to get prepared for what is going to come.

When attempting this stage, you should be sealed somewhere around Lv.30, so the enemies will be rather weak compared to your cats. There are many units who can get to Henry's blind spot because there is no "big" unit to help him. (Except for Dolphina, but she conveniently has a blind spot too.) If your units barely cannot reach Henry's blind spot, use [[Ototo Corps|Thunderbolt]] cannon.

This level becomes a cakewalk if you own [[Baby Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Baby Cat]]. Not only is it Freeze Immune, but it also has wave attacks which help kill multiple enemies at once and snipe Dolphina.

